## 3.13 Engineering Notes

### Purpose

The Engineering Notes section records supplementary engineering information that supports the understanding, interpretation, or future evolution of a System Objective.

Its purpose is to preserve valuable engineering knowledge while ensuring that the formal objective remains concise, stable, and solution-independent.

---

### Standard Fields

Every System Objective may include the following fields where applicable:

| Field | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| Engineering Observation | Relevant observations supporting the objective. |
| Engineering Considerations | Important considerations for future engineering activities. |
| Assumptions | Additional assumptions not included elsewhere. |
| Known Limitations | Identified limitations relevant to the objective. |
| Future Considerations | Potential future enhancements or areas requiring further investigation. |

---

### Engineering Notes Rules

Engineering Notes shall:

- Support, but not modify, the formal Objective Statement.
- Remain technically relevant.
- Avoid introducing new requirements.
- Avoid prescribing implementation methods unless explicitly authorized.
- Be reviewed whenever the objective is revised.

---

### Engineering Note

Engineering Notes preserve valuable engineering knowledge that may assist future engineers in understanding the context of an objective.

They are informative rather than normative and shall not be interpreted as additional engineering requirements.
